{
  "$comment": "The reference set of spec 00020 §7.1: every family, every table state a token indexer has to render. Each row is one contract deployment plus the ordered steps taken against it. `domain` and `piece` strings are passed through Compact's pad(32, …); `name` and `symbol` are padded to 32 bytes each. Every metadata step carries the `valType` of MIP section 2.1 (1 UTF-8 string, 2 unsigned integer, 3 JSON, 4 absolute URI), which is what the generator writes into the payload's type byte. This file drives scripts/export-simulator-fixtures.ts and scripts/generate-literal-contracts.ts, and is the seed for the on-chain deployment matrix.",
  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "LSUN",
      "name": "Ledger Sun",
      "symbol": "LSUN",
      "decimals": 6,
      "kind": 2,
      "template": "LedgerToken",
      "domain": "umbra:lsun",
      "expect": { "status": "declared", "storage": "ledger", "color": null, "mintCount": 0 },
      "steps": [
        { "op": "publishMetadata" },
        { "op": "ledgerMint", "to": "owner", "amount": "1000000" },
        { "op": "transfer", "to": "holder:lsun-1", "amount": "250000" }
      ]
    },
    {
